abstract: >-
  Large Electronic Loads (LELs), such as data centers, are rapidly becoming a dominant share of bulk power system
  load, with ride-through and reconnection behavior unlike conventional motor-driven load. NERC's May 2026 Level 3
  Alert directs Transmission Planners and Planning Coordinators to use the PERC1 model, or an equivalent-or-better
  model, as the baseline for large load modeling, but these models' many parameters and cease/reconnect options make
  consistent parameterization difficult without facility-level power electronics data. PERC Studio is a desktop
  studio that accelerates data center modeling for transmission planning engineers. From a facility's ride-through
  standard and equipment type, or full field-measured CON values for as-built facilities, it produces a ready-to-use
  PSS/E .dyr file and an HTML report documenting assumptions and plotting simulated ride-through performance live
  against a library of independently sourced ride-through presets (three generic tiers plus grid-operator standards
  such as ERCOT NOGRR282, MISO, SPP HILL, and NERC PRC-029-1 and the LLWG SAR proposal).
